!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-template-family-members.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A template is not a type, so a family whose members are applications is based on a record ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10).
  `boxed` is the abstract base, `box` composes it, and `bt` declares an application of `box`, which IS-A `boxed`
  through `box`'s written parent. A position typed `boxed` dispatches by tag over the declared members.
  """
!schema {
  boxed  => abstract { }
  box    => <T> boxed & { v: T }
  bt     => box<int32>
  holder => { any: boxed }
}
